.TH ESDM\-PROC 8 "2026-08-05" "ESDM @VERSION@" "ESDM Manual"
.SH NAME
esdm\-proc \- serve /proc/sys/kernel/random from the ESDM
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B esdm\-proc
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.I MOUNTPOINT
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B esdm\-proc
is a FUSE file system that provides the interface applications know as
.I /proc/sys/kernel/random
with values taken from
.BR esdm\-server (8)
instead of from the kernel RNG. It is normally mounted over the kernel's own
directory, so that entropy gathering daemons and other consumers reading those
files see the state of the ESDM.
.PP
The following files are served:
.TP
.I boot_id
The boot ID, stable for the lifetime of the daemon.
.TP
.I uuid
A freshly generated random UUID on every read.
.TP
.I entropy_avail
Entropy currently held by the ESDM, in bits.
.TP
.I poolsize
Size of the entropy pool, in bits.
.TP
.I write_wakeup_threshold
Entropy level below which writers polling the random device are woken.
Writable.
.TP
.I urandom_min_reseed_secs
Minimum number of seconds between two reseed operations. Zero reseeds before
every request. Writable.
.TP
.I esdm_type
Identifies the provider as the ESDM. This file has no counterpart in the
kernel and lets a consumer tell the two apart.
.PP
The daemon needs to be started as root to mount over
.IR /proc/sys/kernel/random .
On systemd installations it is normally started through the shipped
.B esdm\-proc.service
unit, which is pulled in by
.BR esdm\-linux\-compat.target .
.PP
The options are handled by FUSE, so the general FUSE mount options are
accepted in addition to the ones listed below. Serving the mount to users
other than the one running the daemon requires the FUSE option
.BR "\-o allow_other" .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbosity= \fINUM\fR
Logging verbosity level.
.TP
.B \-\-relabel
Perform automatic SELinux relabeling of the served files, so that they carry
the same context as the kernel files they replace.
.TP
.B \-\-syslog
Log via syslog.
.SH EXAMPLES
Mount over the kernel directory the way the shipped service unit does:
.PP
.RS
.nf
esdm\-proc \-\-relabel \-\-syslog \-f \-o allow_other /proc/sys/kernel/random \-v 3
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR esdm\-server (8),
.BR esdm\-cuse\-random (8),
.BR esdm\-tool (1),
.BR random (4),
.BR fuse (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Stephan Mueller <smueller@chronox.de>
